7592186045499 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446390 1083 #uuid "ba1f709b-6e8f-51a1-8804-ab7f3827078d" 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446391 1080 "II and IV only" 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446391 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446391 1083 #uuid "d31db710-ba28-5d15-bc4f-73b558920048" 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446392 1080 "I, II, and III only" 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446392 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446392 1083 #uuid "d3c0835e-5f1d-544e-a853-45dfc3915a23" 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446393 1080 "IV only" 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446393 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446393 1083 #uuid "f2c27ec0-cc47-51bf-badb-c070af87e34b" 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446394 1080 "I and IV only" 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446394 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446394 1083 #uuid "f39e815a-9af1-5b99-ab72-d96f070a17af" 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446395 1080 "I and IV only" 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446395 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446395 1083 #uuid "ff6b6d03-54db-5749-ac52-1169cfe1be1b" 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446396 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446382 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446396 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446383 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446396 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446386 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446396 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446387 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446396 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446389 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446396 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446396 1077 "selection" 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446396 1078 #edb/ref 17592186446387 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446396 1079 #uuid "17130b31-13ec-59ea-9907-9dc1bafa977c" 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446397 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446384 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446397 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446385 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446397 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446390 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446397 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446393 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446397 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446394 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446397 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446397 1077 "selection" 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446397 1078 #edb/ref 17592186446393 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446397 1079 #uuid "50cbeb90-f349-5abb-ae1c-099b501ea736" 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446398 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446381 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446398 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446388 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446398 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446391 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446398 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446392 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446398 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446395 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446398 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446398 1077 "selection" 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446398 1078 #edb/ref 17592186446392 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446398 1079 #uuid "69df5860-5124-59d0-9e37-9e55acc83e24" 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446399 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446397 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446399 1069 "q-107146" 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446399 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446399 1071 "Consider the vector space $C[-1,1]$ of all continuous functions $f:[-1,1]\\to R$ and its subset $B=\\{f\\in C[-1,1]\\,|\\,f(1)\\ne f(-1)\\}.$ \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $B$ is closed under function addition\n\nII. $B$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n\nIII. $B$ is a subspace of $C[-1,1]$\n\nIV. $B$ is **not** a subspace of $C[-1,1]$" 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446399 1072 #uuid "33331944-2261-5079-a111-5d0397fe6a4a" 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446399 1074 "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, if  $f(x)=x$ and $g(x)=-x,$ then $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ are in $B,$ but\n\n$$\n(f+g)(x)=x-x=0\n$$\n\n for all $x\\in [0,1].$\nIn particular, \n\n$$\n(f+g)(1)=(f+g)(-1).\n$$\n\n So, $f+g\\notin B.$ Hence, $B$ is *not* closed under function addition.\n\n- Statement II is false. If $f(x)\\in B$ and $k=0,$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kf(1) & =0\\cdot f(1) \\\\  & =0 \\\\  & =0\\cdot f(-1) \\\\  & =(kf)(-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $kf\\notin B.$ Hence, $B$ is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $B$ is *not* a subspace because it's not closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"IV only.\"" 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446400 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446398 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446400 1069 "q-107103" 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446400 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446400 1071 "Consider the vector space ${R}_{2}[t]$ of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $2,$ and its subset $A$ containing all polynomials of the form $at-b,$ where $a,b\\in R.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ is closed under polynomial addition\n\nII. $A$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n\nIII. $A$ is a subspace of ${R}_{2}[t]$\n\nIV. $A$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}_{2}[t]$" 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446400 1072 #uuid "645fccc2-d171-5fdf-83e7-9f6a35f005d6" 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446400 1074 "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If $f(t)={a}_{1}t-{b}_{1}$ and $g(t)={a}_{2}t-{b}_{2}$ are two polynomials from $A,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)+g(t) & =({a}_{1}t-{b}_{1})+({a}_{2}t-{b}_{2}) \\\\  & =({a}_{1}+{a}_{2})t-({b}_{1}+{b}_{2}),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a polynomial from $A.$ So, $A$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $f(t)=at-b\\in A$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kf(t) & =k(at-b) \\\\  & =(ka)t-(kb),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a polynomial from $A.$ So, $A$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true while statement IV is false. $A$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\"" 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446401 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446396 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446401 1069 "q-107145" 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446401 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446401 1071 "Consider the vector space $C[0,1]$ of all continuous functions $f:[0,1]\\to R$ and its subset $G=\\{f\\in C[0,1]\\,|\\,f(0)\\ge 0\\}.$ \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $G$ is closed under function addition\n\nII. $G$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n\nIII. $G$ is a subspace of $C[0,1]$\n\nIV. $G$ is **not** a subspace of $C[0,1]$" 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446401 1072 #uuid "7e86fe7b-82ad-5786-81ac-5ea87b6be543" 13194139534975 17592186045417 true] [17592186446401 1074 "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, if $f(x),g(x)\\in G,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f+g)(0) & =f(0)+g(0) \\\\  & \\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $G$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, if $f(x)=1$ for all $x\\in [0,1]$ and $k=-1\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(kf)(0) & =((-1)f)(0) \\\\  & =-f(0) \\\\  & =-1 \\\\  & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $G$ is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $G$ is *not* a subspace because it's not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and IV only.\"" 13194139534975 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-02490bd0-71b5-513c-b520-c0758ef51227" 17592186446381 "answer-3829f03a-07c9-5578-b4ae-972b6075fce1" 17592186446382 "answer-40374cb8-c538-5fe0-94c9-123e108a0c2d" 17592186446383 "answer-418823f2-2b02-5914-8925-5d36dd36d6ce" 17592186446384 "answer-77eb99e8-733d-5d18-a9f7-b73130eeaa2b" 17592186446385 "answer-7e051e5b-7291-5e6a-843b-e237005f233c" 17592186446386 "answer-81225a5a-eed1-5477-b5f6-02fdcd401991" 17592186446387 "answer-97e47326-ad4c-525e-b1f6-f379fa5508f3" 17592186446388 "answer-ac35a2f0-ba68-50d8-9b85-dec3524e6bf3" 17592186446389 "answer-ba1f709b-6e8f-51a1-8804-ab7f3827078d" 17592186446390 "answer-d31db710-ba28-5d15-bc4f-73b558920048" 17592186446391 "answer-d3c0835e-5f1d-544e-a853-45dfc3915a23" 17592186446392 "answer-f2c27ec0-cc47-51bf-badb-c070af87e34b" 17592186446393 "answer-f39e815a-9af1-5b99-ab72-d96f070a17af" 17592186446394 "answer-ff6b6d03-54db-5749-ac52-1169cfe1be1b" 17592186446395 "answer-field-17130b31-13ec-59ea-9907-9dc1bafa977c" 17592186446396 "answer-field-50cbeb90-f349-5abb-ae1c-099b501ea736" 17592186446397 "answer-field-69df5860-5124-59d0-9e37-9e55acc83e24" 17592186446398 "question-33331944-2261-5079-a111-5d0397fe6a4a" 17592186446399 "question-645fccc2-d171-5fdf-83e7-9f6